        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "items": [
          "Product mix shift (~$310K): Higher sales of the entry-level line versus the premium line. Revenue grew 4% in Q3 but the blended margin rate dropped 1.2 points because of the volume weighting.",
          "Freight (~$180K): Carrier rate increases took effect mid-Q2; Q3 absorbed the full quarter at the higher rates, plus two expedited shipments tied to customer commitments.",
          "June rebate (~$18K): A vendor rebate credit was received after the Q2 statements cut and was rebooked into June per the accrual policy, which flattered Q2's margin. No similar credit landed in Q3."
        ]
      },
